{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Complementary_Counting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When a certain unfair die is rolled, an even number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times as likely to appear as an odd number. The die is rolled twice. What is the probability that the sum of the numbers rolled is even?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f624cd9ee992639f15e6a8d5c1131b51c4d53a14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{3}{8}  \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\  \\frac{4}{9} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\  \\frac{5}{9} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\  \\frac{9}{16} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"380\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since an even number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times more likely to appear than an odd number, the probability of an even number appearing is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />. Since the problem states that the sum of the two die must be even, the numbers must both be even or both be odd. We either have EE or OO, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9df2f4f8f0bd33c690522e4a4abce345ead2579.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4} + \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac {1}{16} + \\frac {9}{16} = \\frac{10}{16} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{8}}.\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~Arcticturn ~Aidensharp\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Complementary_Counting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Complementary_Counting)\">Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As explained in the above solution, the probability of an even number appearing is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />, while the probability of an odd number appearing is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Then the probability of getting an odd and an even (to make an odd number) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8d4f0190d3e76b206cc1ae34d62def02ff9449.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 2 = \\frac{3}{8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" /> Then the probability of getting an even number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/721c27b8002b7c689210ce08c2e2d3a39bbc4516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\frac{3}{8} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{8}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"133\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~littlefox_amc\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 3 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As explained in the above solutions, the probability of an even number appearing is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />. Getting two even numbers in a row would result in an even sum, and the probability of this happening is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128cd150280f5c3bb27c3b8b4827ee440f38a393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{9}{16}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" /> As an even sum can also be a result of the sum of two odd numbers, the probability of an even sum is slightly greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e5c3537a3e4f3280801505c18d990e821ead3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />. The only answer choice with a probability greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e5c3537a3e4f3280801505c18d990e821ead3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac2fcee17701a3cd8fcf9cbe32d1d6c5b1899d4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{8}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"64\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~TheGoldenRetriever\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<pre><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/xZo7pKxrnGA\">https://youtu.be/xZo7pKxrnGA</a>\n</pre>\n<p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ycRZHCOKTVk?t=661\">https://youtu.be/ycRZHCOKTVk?t=661</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/oOKx2Wqp_ig\">https://youtu.be/oOKx2Wqp_ig</a> ~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editse